## Getting Started
### Client Library
```
import { fal } from "@fal-ai/client";

fal.config({
     // Can also be auto-configured using environment variables:
     credentials: "FAL_KEY",
});
```

### The fal client proxy
```
export { handler as default } from "@fal-ai/server-proxy/nextjs";
```

```
import { fal } from "@fal-ai/client";
fal.config({
     proxyUrl: "/api/fal/proxy",
});
```

## [​](https://fal.ai/docs/documentation/model-apis/inference/synchronous#using-subscribe-queue-backed)  Using `subscribe` (Queue-backed)
```
import fal_client

result = fal_client.subscribe("fal-ai/flux/schnell", arguments={
    "prompt": "a sunset over mountains"
})

print(result["images"][0]["url"])
```

```
import asyncio
import fal_client

async def main():
    result = await fal_client.subscribe_async("fal-ai/flux/schnell", arguments={
        "prompt": "a sunset over mountains"
    })
    print(result["images"][0]["url"])

asyncio.run(main())
```

```
import { fal } from "@fal-ai/client";

const result = await fal.subscribe("fal-ai/flux/schnell", {
  input: { prompt: "a sunset over mountains" }
});

console.log(result.data.images[0].url);
```

## [​](https://fal.ai/docs/documentation/model-apis/inference/synchronous#subscribe-parameters)  `subscribe()` Parameters
### [​](https://fal.ai/docs/documentation/model-apis/inference/synchronous#on_enqueue)  `on_enqueue`
```
def save_request_id(request_id):
    print(f"Enqueued: {request_id}")

result = fal_client.subscribe(
    "fal-ai/nano-banana-2",
    arguments={"prompt": "a sunset"},
    on_enqueue=save_request_id,
)
```

```
const result = await fal.subscribe("fal-ai/nano-banana-2", {
  input: { prompt: "a sunset" },
  onEnqueue: (requestId) => {
    console.log(`Enqueued: ${requestId}`);
  },
});
```

### [​](https://fal.ai/docs/documentation/model-apis/inference/synchronous#on_queue_update-/-onqueueupdate)  `on_queue_update` / `onQueueUpdate`
```
const result = await fal.subscribe("fal-ai/nano-banana-2", {
  input: { prompt: "a sunset" },
  logs: true,
  onQueueUpdate: (update) => {
    if (update.status === "IN_QUEUE") {
      console.log(`Position: ${update.queue_position}`);
    } else if (update.status === "IN_PROGRESS") {
      update.logs?.forEach(log => console.log(log.message));
    }
  },
});
```

